
config PHOSPHOR_USER_MANAGER
    bool "openbmc phosphor-user-manager"

config PHOSPHOR_USER_MANAGER_SELFTEST
    bool "run the phosphor-user-manager D-Bus self test at boot"
    depends on PHOSPHOR_USER_MANAGER
    help
      Start a thread that waits for the D-Bus broker and the User.Manager
      service, then exercises the full D-Bus API (CreateUser/GetUserInfo/
      RenameUser/DeleteGroup/AccountPolicy/...) the way other services do
      and prints PASS/FAIL per case.

config PHOSPHOR_USER_MANAGER_SELFTEST_DISCONNECT_BUG
    bool "reproduce the dbus-broker disconnect bug in the self test"
    depends on PHOSPHOR_USER_MANAGER_SELFTEST
    help
      After the self test, call disconnect_from_dbroker() like the earlier
      code did.  That returns the socketpair to the broker pool and corrupts
      the broker: the next client connection (ipmi_thread) makes the broker
      thread fault and then the other D-Bus threads die with it.  Enable this
      to reproduce the bug for the fix; leave it off for a usable test image.
